================================================================================================
   (a) capacitor charged by I = 1.0 A: conduction current through flat disk = 1.0 A, through bag in the gap = 0 A; displacement through the bag = dQ/dt = 1.0 A -> conduction alone is surface dependent: FALSE
   [ok] (c) div(curl F) at random point 1: computed 0  expected 0
   [ok] (c) div(curl F) at random point 2: computed 5.551115123e-13  expected 0
   (c) 0 = div J + d(div D)/dt = div J + d rho/dt: TRUE
   (d) B = B0 (x,y,z) static: div B = 3.000000 B0 (nonzero, constant in time); d(div B)/dt = 0 is satisfied with E = 0, yet div B != 0 -> Faraday alone does not force div B = 0: FALSE
   (e) rectangle 1 m long, w = 1e-02 m: displacement current through it = 7.0e-02 A -> 0 as w -> 0: FALSE
   (e) rectangle 1 m long, w = 1e-04 m: displacement current through it = 7.0e-04 A -> 0 as w -> 0: FALSE
   (e) rectangle 1 m long, w = 1e-06 m: displacement current through it = 7.0e-06 A -> 0 as w -> 0: FALSE
   (b) eps0 dE/dt is nonzero in vacuum whenever E changes: TRUE
   ANSWER 16.4: (a) F, (b) T, (c) T, (d) F, (e) F
